uation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-6x+12y & =7 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(0)^{2}-6x+12(0) & =7 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x & =7 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x+9)-9 & =7 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{16} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-1,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(-1,0)$ and $(7,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290964 #edb/ref 1080 "1-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290964 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290964 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4da3d003-4066-5e13-a990-aa06c67ebbb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291122 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291122 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291122 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "722eea0d-ffa4-5e80-8aec-27119ee94edf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291210 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291210 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291210 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "876ce42f-4d4b-5ff4-9bba-e69a11cf3a9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291412 #edb/ref 1080 "1+\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291412 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291412 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b29f354d-93d3-58cc-aec0-e2dc74bff0a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291936 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291936 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291936 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291936 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186290964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291936 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3b62c011-8d8e-52e4-882b-5f186531492c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292212 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292212 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 1759218604549