-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}+14{y}^{2}-50x-11y & =29 \\\\ 25{x}^{2}+14(0)^{2}-50x-11(0) & =29 \\\\ 25{x}^{2}-50x & =29 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x & =\\frac{29}{25} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2} & =\\frac{29}{25} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{29}{25}+1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{29}{25}+\\frac{25}{25} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{54}{25} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are\n\n$$\nA(1-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5},0)\\,\\text{and}\\,B(1+\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{5},0).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300098 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300098 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300098 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d245bd1-16b6-5012-a8d9-04904c36e4c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300355 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300355 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300355 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b9ad17a-08c5-549d-bdca-ef656f5b4921" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300581 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300581 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300581 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7c506244-23a8-501d-b5b4-52708d2ca4b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300858 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300858 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300858 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b42abee5-d9b5-5350-b275-d5c52870eead" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301559 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301559 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301559 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301559 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301559 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "68e33511-4f81-5c80-923e-e15b804a92f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301597 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301597 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301597 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301597 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301597 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "77a6ead7-3faa-53ce-955a-2c79a8fa6193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301793 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301793 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301793 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301793 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ae584667-f653-502a-8a6d-e9a67817154d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301861 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301861 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301861 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301861 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c2a331de-b101-5cb3-b886-0857e82653de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302227 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302227 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302227 #edb/ref 1069 "q-325860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302227 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302227 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the point where the ellipse $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{36}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis.\n\nThe $x$-intercept is $($\n{{field-1}}\n,\n{{field-2}}$).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302227 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6faabf38-ea7b-5072-9ed7-46de60d9b5e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302227 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0-6)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{36}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9} & =0 \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x+3 & =0 \\\\ x & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the point $(-3,0).$\n\n![](images/5a/5a1377fa0ff46ff7a7e4b685d38852ad67abd8c0adfc432fc22d7c1d57b7a57f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302260 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302260 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302260 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326043" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302260 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302260 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the point where the ellipse  $9{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+18x+32y+9=0$ intercepts the $x$-axis.\n\nThe $x$-intercept is $($\n{{field-1}}\n,\n{{field-2}}$).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302260 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99df4a96-1be0-51fa-912f-796019bd7b76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302260 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+18x+32y+9 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}+8\\cdot {0}^{2}+18x+32\\cdot 0+9 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}+18x+9 & =0 \\\\ 9\\,[{x}^{2}+2x]+9 & =0 \\\\ 9[(x+1)^{2}-1]+9 & =0 \\\\ 9(x+1)^{2}-9+9 & =0 \\\\ 9(x+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at  $(-1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358299 #edb/ref 1080 "$(2,0)$ and $(4,0)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358299 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186